# Narrator: a guest who keeps out of fights (docs/contracts/campaign.md: her NPC's guest_fights false: Ireena, then Gertruda).
# LocationFights says combat:keeps_back:<npc>:first once, as the first fight begins with her along, and
# combat:keeps_back:<npc> in later fights (it holds off for a while between them), a beat after the fight's own opening
# line. Combat lines are one sentence under 15 words; the first may run to two. Drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge
# (docs/plans/gemini_allies/E3/: brief, raw reply, what was changed), edited for length and canon. Unvoiced for now. The last
# four of her lines are package I4's (docs/plans/gemini_allies/i4/): what she does from the back of a fight.

~ combat:keeps_back:ireena:first
| Ireena steps back, blade sheathed. What comes for you goes round her like water round a stone, as if it had been told whose she is.
once

~ combat:keeps_back:ireena
| Ireena's knuckles whiten on her sheathed hilt as she steps clear of the steel.
| Hungry eyes slide right past Ireena to fix on you alone.
| Ireena folds her arms over her cloak, watching every blow she cannot answer.
| Not one blade angles toward Ireena where she waits.
| Ireena measures the distance between your back and the dark with level eyes.
| Ireena's sharp warning cuts through the clash of steel to guard your blind side.
| Ireena calls out across the din, and a blade turns just in time.
| Ireena weighs a road-stone in her palm, then lets it drop.
| Ireena holds the lantern high, casting steady light across the ground where you fight.
cooldown 20

# Gertruda (docs/story/gertruda_noncombatant.md): the same rule for Mad Mary's daughter while the party takes her home. The valley
# is not told whose she is, so nothing explains why a blow never turns on her; she only stands very still. Drafted by Gemini through
# the ai-bridge (docs/plans/gemini_allies/gertruda/: briefs, raw replies, what was changed), edited for canon and length. Unvoiced.

~ combat:keeps_back:gertruda:first
| Gertruda steps back behind you and goes still, her hands folded in the skirts of her borrowed gown. Nothing in the fight so much as glances her way.
once

~ combat:keeps_back:gertruda
| Gertruda gathers her borrowed skirts in both fists and stands well back.
| The tune in Gertruda's throat dies as she settles into the quiet.
| Well behind your shoulder, Gertruda keeps the stillness she knows best.
| Gertruda watches the first blow fall without a sound or a step.
| Gertruda presses both hands over her ears and waits like a carved stone.
| Gertruda shuts her eyes tight, then opens them to watch in silence.
| Gertruda swallows a small gasp and fixes her gaze upon her shoes.
| Gertruda stares down at the hem of her borrowed gown, utterly still.
| Gertruda clasps her cold hands together, keeping as quiet as a shadow.
cooldown 20
